    "×%lld" : {

    },
    "A book keeps going. There is no route and no finish line; you just add plates to it, on a road trip or on the way to work. Starting one never touches the books you already have." : {

    },
    "A nudge if a trip goes a day without a plate." : {

    },
    "A party is for one car. Everybody opens Plates, one person starts it, the rest join over the local network, and the same drive is scored on every phone with a colored corner on each tile showing who called it. No account and no signal needed." : {

    },
    "A plate keeps the value it had when you called it. Driving on afterwards never quietly rewrites what a find was worth." : {

    },
    "A shared book is for people who are not together. Invite somebody from a book you own and you both add plates to it from wherever you are, over iCloud." : {

    },
    "A state stays open after the first person calls it, so it counts for all of you." : {

    },
    "A trip is one drive with a route and a finish. A book you just keep adding to." : {

    },
    "A trip is one drive with a route and a finish. A book you just keep adding to. Pick one to start collecting. You can have both later." : {

    },
    "A trip is one drive. It has a route, it has a finish, and its score is about that journey. A book never ends — it is the one you keep in the car and fill over years." : {

    },
    "A trip is one journey: it has a route, and it ends. For everyday spotting on the way to school or the shops, use a plate book instead: it just keeps going." : {

